   $q$Why does Lena walk ahead of the tractor on the third day?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is tired of riding the fender and wants to go back to the house early.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She gives him a steady pace to follow, a quiet way of guiding him without pressure.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She is checking the soybean rows for damage the tractor caused.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She has given up on him and is leaving the field so he must quit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She gives him a steady pace to follow, a quiet way of guiding him without pressure.$q$, $q$After she walks ahead, he "followed her slow steps along the rows" and the engine "held," so her walk gives him something calm to follow. She turns back "almost smiling," which shows she has not given up.$q$, 'draft', '1e97858a-fa63-5466-bfac-59a51c9825b3')
