   $q$What do the lines "I think she had decided I was worth her mornings. / I think I had decided to deserve it." suggest about how the two characters have changed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Her growing respect and his growing effort have changed each other.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Lena has become a better driver than before by teaching her brother.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Both of them now regret the week and wish their father had stayed home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The speaker now believes he is a better farmer than his older sister.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her growing respect and his growing effort have changed each other.$q$, $q$The paired lines show a two-way change: she now values the time spent on him, and he now works to earn that respect. Nothing in the poem suggests he thinks he is better than Lena.$q$, 'draft', '1e97858a-fa63-5466-bfac-59a51c9825b3')
