   $q$Why is Pell first drawn to the clock tower?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She wants to learn how to keep the town's time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"},{"text":"She wants to wake the owl and play a trick on him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She loves the shining brass pins and gears.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She is looking for a safe place to build a nest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She loves the shining brass pins and gears.$q$, $q$Pell admires the tower because "the gears shone" and "nothing in her nest was half so bright." She only learns about timekeeping at the very end, after the trouble she causes.$q$, 'draft', 'f602dc38-6f57-521f-9030-c7c6764339da')
