   $q$What happens as a result of Pell taking the pins?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ormond leaves the tower to live somewhere quieter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The tower collapses and the gears fall into the square.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"},{"text":"The bells ring at the wrong hour and confuse the town.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bells stop ringing completely for a whole month.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-details"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bells ring at the wrong hour and confuse the town.$q$, $q$The bells "rang at the wrong hour," so the baker, children, and farmers all get the time wrong. The clock is not destroyed and the bells do not go silent; the month is how long Pell later studies with Ormond.$q$, 'draft', 'f602dc38-6f57-521f-9030-c7c6764339da')
