   $q$How does Esther know that the headline is wrong?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mr. Halvorsen tells her he was not sure of the name.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She was at the spelling bee and saw who actually won.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Clara Adeyemi comes to the newspaper office to complain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She compares the proof to an earlier copy of the paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She was at the spelling bee and saw who actually won.$q$, $q$Esther "had been in the town hall that afternoon" and watched Ruth miss "rhythm," so she knows Clara won. No one comes to complain and Mr. Halvorsen never admits doubt.$q$, 'draft', 'be92127d-d0c9-54f5-80f6-b8ebc41372f7')
