  ('fc00eb89-c07a-532f-8726-be5299dbf773', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-character-setting-plot'), null, 'hard',
   $q$What does Mr. Halvorsen's choice to pull the lever reveal about him?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He secretly knew about the error all along and was testing Esther's attention.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Though stern and proud, he cares more about printing the truth than about his pride.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He is easily frightened by his apprentice and gives in to avoid an argument.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"He wants to finish the night's work quickly so he can go home and rest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Though stern and proud, he cares more about printing the truth than about his pride.$q$, $q$He frowns and is a man who "trusted no one's eyes but his own," yet he stops the press and loses three hundred sheets to fix the name. They work until "nearly two in the morning," so he is not rushing home.$q$, 'draft', 'be92127d-d0c9-54f5-80f6-b8ebc41372f7')
